## 4. Database (SQLite — `app.db`)

### Schema Overview

```sql
users          (id, name, email, password_hash, created_at)
sessions       (token PK, user_id FK, created_at)
complaints     (id, user_id FK, text, ward, category, confidence,
                department, status DEFAULT 'Submitted', created_at)
notifications  (id, user_id FK, complaint_id, title, message,
                is_read DEFAULT 0, created_at)
reports        (id, user_id FK, title, text, category, confidence,
                department, city, area, lat, lng,
                status DEFAULT 'open', embedding BLOB,
                created_at, updated_at)
checks         (id, report_id FK, user_id FK, kind, note,
                created_at, UNIQUE(report_id, user_id))
```

### Key Design Decisions
- **`reports.embedding BLOB`** — The sentence vector is stored as raw `float32` bytes directly in SQLite. This lets the live FAISS index be **rebuilt from the database** every time the server restarts — no separate file needed.
- **`checks` UNIQUE constraint** — Prevents double-checking: `ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE` replaces the previous check.
- Status indexes (`idx_reports_status`, `idx_checks_report`) exist for query performance.
- **Foreign keys are enabled** via `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON` on every connection (important — SQLite doesn't enable this by default).

